※ pl4g-test: compile=error
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 4906 LANG_CLAUSE_NOT_A_TRUTH

※ A condition is evaluated and the program stops where it does not hold, so
※ what it comes to has to be a truth.  Nothing is converted: an integer is not
※ a condition here, exactly as it is not in an `if`.

fn step(a: u8) → u8 pre(a):
    a

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    ⎕narrow(step(1u8), ⌜u6⌝) ?? 1u6
